{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGaugeFixing","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGaugeFixing","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":27,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.trefoil_transversePairing_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.trefoil_transversePairing_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":306,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermRootVectorGaugeFixing.lean#L306-L314","doc":"The genus-one trefoil specialisation with the standard Seifert intersection\nform `J = V - Vᵀ = !![0, 1; -1, 0]` and the derived handle exponents\n`(1, 2)` (the partial products before bands 2 and 3 of `σ₁³`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.deuteron_transversePairing_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.deuteron_transversePairing_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermRootVectorGaugeFixing.lean#L288-L304","doc":"**THE DEUTERON RESULT.**\n\nOn the `pn`/deuteron channel word `σ₁³` every admissible handle transport is\na power of `ρ(σ₁)`, and the germ curvature is an `Ad(ρ(σ₁))`-eigenvector.\nHence the transverse non-abelian-Stokes surface pairing vanishes — for\n**every** Seifert intersection form `J` and **every** handle-exponent\nassignment `k`.\n\nThe `0 … 897` spread reported by the trefoil discretization probe therefore\ndoes not measure a physical ambiguity; the admissible sub-orbit is a single\npoint, and it is `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.isRootVector_germCurvature","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.isRootVector_germCurvature","kind":"theorem","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermRootVectorGaugeFixing.lean#L284-L286","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.heckeUnit1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.heckeUnit1","kind":"def","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermRootVectorGaugeFixing.lean#L279-L282","doc":"`ρ(σ₁)` as a unit of the matrix ring — the transport unit of the deuteron\nchannel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.germCurvature_conj_heckeGen1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.germCurvature_conj_heckeGen1","kind":"theorem","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermRootVectorGaugeFixing.lean#L265-L277","doc":"**THE ROOT-VECTOR IDENTITY.** `Ad(σ₁) F_q = (-q²) • F_q`.\n\nThe germ `q`-curvature is an eigenvector of conjugation by the Hecke\ngenerator, with eigenvalue the ratio of `σ₁`'s eigenvalues,\n`q / (-q⁻¹) = -q²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.germCurvature_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.germCurvature_sq","kind":"theorem","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermRootVectorGaugeFixing.lean#L257-L263","doc":"**The germ curvature is nilpotent** — the hallmark of a root vector (a\nCartan component would square to a nonzero multiple of the identity). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.germCurvature_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.germCurvature_eq","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermRootVectorGaugeFixing.lean#L251-L255","doc":"**The germ curvature is the pure root vector `-4E`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.heckeGen1_logDeriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.heckeGen1_logDeriv","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermRootVectorGaugeFixing.lean#L239-L249","doc":"**The logarithmic `q`-derivative germ is the constant matrix `H - 2E`.**\n\n`q · (∂_q σ₁) · σ₁⁻¹ = !![1, -2; 0, -1]` — the `q`-dependence cancels\nexactly. This is the Lean-checked half of the germ identification; the\n`∂_q` step itself is the by-hand seam recorded in the module docstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.heckeGen1_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.heckeGen1_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermRootVectorGaugeFixing.lean#L230-L237","doc":"**Hecke relation** `(σ₁ - q)(σ₁ + q⁻¹) = 0` — certifies the eigenvalue pair\n`(q, -q⁻¹)`, i.e. that this is the *Hecke* quotient, not just Burau. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.heckeGen_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.heckeGen_braid","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermRootVectorGaugeFixing.lean#L220-L228","doc":"**Braid relation** `σ₁σ₂σ₁ = σ₂σ₁σ₂` — certifies that `heckeGen1`,\n`heckeGen2` really are a braid-group representation (not arbitrary\nmatrices). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.heckeGen1Inv_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.heckeGen1Inv_mul","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermRootVectorGaugeFixing.lean#L213-L218","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.heckeGen1_mul_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.heckeGen1_mul_inv","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermRootVectorGaugeFixing.lean#L206-L211","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.germCurvature","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.germCurvature","kind":"def","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermRootVectorGaugeFixing.lean#L203-L204","doc":"The germ `q`-curvature `F_q = ⁅δq₁, δq₂⁆`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.germTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.germTwo","kind":"def","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermRootVectorGaugeFixing.lean#L200-L201","doc":"The second germ `δq₂ = -H`, a **constant** (`q`-independent) matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.germOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.germOne","kind":"def","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermRootVectorGaugeFixing.lean#L197-L198","doc":"The first germ `δq₁ = H - 2E`, a **constant** (`q`-independent) matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.dHeckeGen1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.dHeckeGen1","kind":"def","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermRootVectorGaugeFixing.lean#L189-L195","doc":"The entrywise `q`-derivative `∂_q ρ(σ₁)`, supplied as data.\n\n**Seam (see the module docstring).** Lean does not differentiate here; this\nis the by-hand entrywise derivative of `heckeGen1` (`∂_q q = 1`,\n`∂_q (-q⁻¹) = q⁻²`, `∂_q 0 = 0`). Everything downstream of it *is* Lean\nalgebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.heckeGen1Inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.heckeGen1Inv","kind":"def","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermRootVectorGaugeFixing.lean#L186-L187","doc":"The inverse of `ρ(σ₁)` (`det = -1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.heckeGen2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.heckeGen2","kind":"def","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermRootVectorGaugeFixing.lean#L183-L184","doc":"`ρ(σ₂)` in the same representation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.heckeGen1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.heckeGen1","kind":"def","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermRootVectorGaugeFixing.lean#L179-L181","doc":"`ρ(σ₁)` in the 2-dimensional Hecke representation of `B₃` (reduced Burau at\n`t = q²`, rescaled by `-1/q`; eigenvalues `q, -q⁻¹`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.transversePairing_genusOne_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.transversePairing_genusOne_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermRootVectorGaugeFixing.lean#L162-L169","doc":"The two-handle (genus-one) specialisation: a Seifert surface with `H₁` rank 2\nand *any* intersection pairing `j` between its two handles. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.transversePairing_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.transversePairing_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermRootVectorGaugeFixing.lean#L137-L160","doc":"**THE GAUGE-FIXING THEOREM.**\n\nLet the curvature `F` be an `Ad u`-eigenvector and let every handle transport\nbe a power of the single unit `u` — the situation forced by a\nsingle-generator braid word. Then the intersection-form-weighted transverse\nsurface pairing\n\n  `Ω₂^⊥ = Σᵢ Σⱼ Jᵢⱼ • ⁅𝓕ᵢ, 𝓕ⱼ⁆`\n\n**vanishes identically**, for *every* intersection form `J` (so every Seifert\nmatrix, every `H₁` basis, every spanning tree) and *every* assignment `k` of\nhandles to word positions.\n\nSo the surface→scalar map is not merely gauge-*fixable* here: its value does\nnot depend on the gauge at all, and that value is `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.comm_smul_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.comm_smul_smul","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermRootVectorGaugeFixing.lean#L130-L135","doc":"**Two scalar multiples of a common element commute.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.transported_eq_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.transported_eq_smul","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermRootVectorGaugeFixing.lean#L110-L128","doc":"**Root-vector transport is scalar.** Conjugating a root vector by any power\nof its transport unit returns a *scalar multiple of the same element*.\n\nThis is the whole gauge-fixing mechanism: the handle holonomy can be any\npower of `u` whatsoever, and the transported curvature still points along\none fixed line. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.IsRootVector","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.IsRootVector","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermRootVectorGaugeFixing.lean#L106-L108","doc":"**`F` is an `Ad u`-eigenvector (a root vector of the transport torus).** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.transported","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.transported","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermRootVectorGaugeFixing.lean#L99-L104","doc":"**Transported curvature.** The curvature `F` parallel-transported back to the\nbasepoint along the `k`-th partial product of a single-generator word:\n`𝓕ₖ = uᵏ · F · u⁻ᵏ`. On the deuteron word `σ₁³` every admissible transport\nhas this shape, with `u = ρ(σ₁)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.comm_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.comm_self","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermRootVectorGaugeFixing.lean#L96-L97","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermRootVectorGauge.comm","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermRootVectorGaugeFixing.lean#L92-L94","doc":"Ring commutator `⁅x, y⁆ = x*y - y*x`. Stated locally so the file does not\ndepend on which `LieRing` instance is in scope for `A`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}